From a3c2c225b449319f8fe053aa9ba2adbdf49645df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <git@volf.co>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:58:34 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] lanes: TF_DS_SPEC_SAMPLE (off by default) gives a sampled
 stream speculative sampling - the accept rule over the target's served p and
 the drafter's proposal q, with q's normaliser Zq read from the noise kernel

A sampled stream's drafted window is drawn row by row with the stream's key, so its drafts are only ever held for
their confidence: the round keeps a draft only when the target's own sample at its parent row happens to equal it.
Speculative sampling makes the drafter pay for itself: the draft x is accepted when a tagged uniform falls under
min(1, p(x)/q(x)) over the target's served distribution p and the drafter's proposal q, and on the first rejection the
row takes a draw from the residual max(p - q, 0) and the path stops there - so a sampled stream's tokens are p's
whatever the drafts did. The seam is verifyFn's per-row loop: rewriting `o.sampled[r]` is enough, because the core's
acceptPath keeps the longest prefix of rows whose tokens match the target's picks. No core, engine, window or wire
change beyond the pass frame's keys.

q is the drafter's softmax(logit / T) over the full vocabulary at the stream's temperature: the draft is the argmax of
logit + T * gumbel, exactly a draw from q, which is what TF_DS_T26_KEYED_DRAFT's kernel already computes. The accept
ratio needs q's normaliser, so `tf_ds_keyed_noise_kernel` now also writes each row's sum of exp(logit / T) - read
while the row is still clean - into a double buffer (block reduction, one atomicAdd a block, zeroed in the pass, so a
captured graph replays it); the Markov loop's per-step gather also gathers those sums from the peer and the pass reads
them once, so Zq is both ranks' columns. A drafted row's q(y) for the target's candidate set comes from a new
`tf_ds_gather_cols_kernel` against the step's logits row (each rank its own columns, -1 elsewhere, the two ranks'
small results exchanged by the same gather), with the keyed Gumbel the kernel added removed on the host - so only
top_k + MARGIN + 1 ids a drafted row cross the link, and only while the switch is on. p is the served distribution
renormalised over what top_p and min_p keep (sampling.zig's candidate and mask arithmetic, now shared with sampleRow,
whose bits are unchanged), and a sampled round with the switch on reads its logits on the host; its greedy streams'
argmax is the same token.

The drafter's, the acceptance test's and the residual draw's keys are three tags mixed into the stream's seed
(sampling.draft_tag, accept_tag, residual_tag), so all three are independent of the sampler's own key and the reply
stays a function of the seed, the position and the token id. TF_DS_SPEC_SAMPLE parses as the series' switches do
(`1` or `on`; unset, `0`, `off` or anything else off) and is refused at start with TF_DS_T26_KEYED_DRAFT (the noise
kernel is shared, the two paths' seeds are not); the flag is in the fingerprint's features (`spec_sample=1;`, named
only when on) so a mismatched pair refuses to run. Off: no new allocation, no new frame bytes, every reply byte for
byte the base one.

LOSSY, twice. A sampled stream's drafted reply no longer equals its undrafted reply for the same seed: it is the same
distribution (p, per row, and the same for the block), not the same tokens - the drafts it accepts are the drafter's,
and the residual draws its own keys. And a sampled reply is no longer reproducible from its seed alone: the drafts'
depth follows the round loop's allocation, so a load change changes which tokens a seed emits (the distribution does
not). Greedy streams are untouched: no drafts, no speculation, the same argmax.

Tests: the accept rule and the residual on toy p and q (q(x) = 0 accepts, p(x) = 0 rejects and takes the residual,
p == q accepts, a draft off p's support takes the residual from p, disjoint supports), the emitted token's histogram
against p over 200K seeds (chi-square, df 3, under the 1% critical value) for one row and for a three-draft block with
the second and third tokens conditioned on the first, the three keys' independence from the sampler's and from each
other, the switch's parse and the T26 refusal, and the features string with spec_sample on. `zig build test` passes.
Not run on a pair: tools/samp_test.py (one prompt, max_tokens 1 then 3, 5000 seeds, DRAFTS=0 against the switch on,
chi-square of the first and the conditioned second and third tokens) is the first live gate.

    The loop covers the drafter's held drafts only (`1 + w.held`): a window that also carries host tokens (a forced or
    copied plan) keeps those rows on the target's own draws, the pre-existing rule for them, and never reads a step's
    logits row past the pass's steps.
